-- title:
--   Regularity at points (b,b^q) with b^{q^2}≠ b
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism which kills exactly the maximal ideal of $A$ (hypothesis `hker`: $\mathrm{red}\,a=0$ iff $a$ lies in that maximal ideal). Let `data` be a modular polynomial datum for $q$, that is a monic $\Phi\in\mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing at $(j,j_q)$ in the sense of `ModularPolynomialData`, and assume Kronecker's congruence `hKr`: the coefficientwise reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(C(X)^q-X)\,(C(X)-X^q)$. Let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that (i) $g$ lies in `modularLocalized (1 * q) A red`, i.e. there are $r,s$ in the subring generated by the constant series of elements of $A$ together with the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at level $1\cdot q$, with the coefficientwise reduction of $s$ under `red` nonzero, and $g\,s=r$; and (ii) $g$ is integral over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[\,$`jqModC`$\,]$. Then for every $x_0\in A$ whose reduction $b=\mathrm{red}\,x_0$ satisfies $b^{q^2}\neq b$, the series $g$ lies in `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A red b (b ^ q)`: there exist two-variable polynomials $r,s$ over $A$ with $\bar s(b,b^q)\neq 0$ in $k$ and $g\cdot s(j,j_q)=r(j,j_q)$, where $s,r$ are evaluated with coefficients reduced by `red` and variables sent to the two $q$-expansions.
--
--   The plane special fibre of the Kronecker model of $X_0(q)$ is $(X^q-Y)(X-Y^q)=0$, and at a point $(b,b^q)$ with $b\notin\mathbb F_{q^2}$ only one branch passes, so regularity along the component at infinity together with integrality over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[j]$ propagates to regularity at that point. It is used in the place-specialisation arguments, namely in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.exists_red_ne_zero_and_coeffEmb_modularUnitSeries_inv_sub_algebraMap_mem_nonunits_of_isStrictTypeOne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.exists_red_ne_zero_and_coeffEmb_modularUnitSeries_inv_sub_algebraMap_mem_nonunits_of_isStrictTypeOne) and [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.red_eq_zero_of_isCuspidal_of_coeffEmb_modularUnitSeries_inv_sub_algebraMap_mem_nonunits`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.red_eq_zero_of_isCuspidal_of_coeffEmb_modularUnitSeries_inv_sub_algebraMap_mem_nonunits).
